{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":56248,"duration_api_ms":56215,"num_turns":9,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"8ca663ea-8c27-4951-9abf-e77988d7875d","total_cost_usd":0.31995300000000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":28882,"cache_read_input_tokens":192211,"output_tokens":1732,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":28882,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":7,"outputTokens":1732,"cacheReadInputTokens":192211,"cacheCreationInputTokens":28882,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.31995300000000004,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Verified both amendments against the codebase. The UI label inconsistency (fr-7-801f49b2) is a real issue: main.rs:597 shows gross volume via geometry.water_volume_l() (22L) as \"Filled volume\" while chemistry uses state.water_volume_l() (19L net). The LEGACY constant doc amendment (fr-7-501d15bd) is based on an incorrect derivation — the default substrate depth is 3.0cm yielding 19L net, not 20L as claimed. Adding a doc comment with a false derivation would be harmful.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-7-801f49b2","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed in the codebase: geometry.water_volume_l() at geometry.rs:19 returns gross filled-prism volume (40×25×22/1000 = 22L for defaults), while state.water_volume_l() at state.rs:177 subtracts substrate displacement (net = 19L with default 3cm substrate). The scenario selection screen at main.rs:597 labels the gross volume as 'Filled volume', which is misleading since all chemistry calculations use the net volume. Users back-calculating concentrations from the displayed volume would get wrong answers. Relabeling as 'Tank capacity' or showing both values is a low-cost fix for a genuine UX inconsistency."},{"amendment_id":"fr-7-501d15bd","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment's derivation is factually incorrect. It claims LEGACY_KINETIC_REFERENCE_VOLUME_L=20.0 comes from '40×25×22/1000 − 40×25×2/1000 = 20L', assuming a 2cm substrate depth. However, the default SubstrateLayerState at substrate.rs:28 has depth_cm = 3.0, yielding net volume = 40×25×(22−3)/1000 = 19L, not 20L. The constant 20.0 does not match the default tank's net water volume under any current configuration. Adding a doc comment asserting this false derivation would be actively misleading — it would give false confidence that the constant is tied to geometry when the math doesn't check out. The origin of the 20.0 value is unclear and a wrong explanation is worse than none."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"d29f5634-b447-493a-87f8-e1026002bfb9"}
